{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional "},{"code":"FirebladeECSMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product provides the "},{"code":"@Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It turns a "},{"code":"struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"enum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into a component and implements a set of component protocols from its stored properties, so you don’t have to write that code by hand:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generated"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enables"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/RegistrableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"componentTypeName"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.register(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.registeredComponentTypes"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.componentType(named:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/CloneableComponent"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"init(cloning:context:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"clone(context:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entity.clone()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.clone(entities:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.clone(into:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SerializableComponent","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CodingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.encodeSnapshot(using:handling:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.restoreSnapshot(from:using:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.decodeSnapshot(from:using:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus: Codable"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/InspectableComponent"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"componentProperties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"generic inspection, e.g. in editors"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/DefaultInitializable"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":" if every stored property has a default value (structs)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"key path assignment, state machines","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Component"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"static let componentIndex","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"typed lookups read a plain static instead of taking the registry lock"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The core ","type":"text"},{"code":"FirebladeECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library stays dependency free. Only ","type":"text"},{"code":"FirebladeECSMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" depends on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-syntax"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"All protocols can also be implemented by hand without the macro.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Adding-the-product","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Adding the product"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to your target. It does not re-export ","type":"text"},{"code":"FirebladeECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FirebladeECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product too and import both modules in every file that uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"YourTargetName\",","    dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECS\", package: \"ecs\"),","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECSMacros\", package: \"ecs\")","    ])"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Declaring-components","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Declaring components"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import FirebladeECS","import FirebladeECSMacros","","@Component","struct Transform {","    var position: SIMD3<Float> = .zero","    var parent: EntityIdentifier?","    @ComponentIgnored var cachedMatrix: [Float] = []  \/\/ still cloned, but not serialized or inspected","}","","@Component(excluding: .serializable)  \/\/ runtime-only component","struct RenderHandle: @unchecked Sendable {","    var handle: Int = 0","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stable type name defaults to the fully qualified type name. Declare ","type":"text"},{"code":"static let componentTypeName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to override it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After renaming a persisted type, list its former names in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let componentTypeNameAliases"},{"type":"text","text":" so existing snapshots keep loading. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component(excluding:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComponentMacroFeatures"},{"type":"text","text":" set: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cloneable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".serializable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inspectable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".defaultInit"},{"type":"text","text":". Registration is always implemented."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ComponentIgnored"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a stored property out of serialization and inspection. Ignored properties are still cloned and need a default value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Serialized properties need an explicit type annotation. ","type":"text"},{"code":"let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constants with an initial value are not serialized.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Members you declare yourself are not generated. Declaring any of ","type":"text"},{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves serialization entirely to you."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated initializers live in an extension, so a struct keeps its memberwise initializer. A "},{"code":"public","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"package","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct, and a struct that declares initializers, gets a generated ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its body (the implicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is internal and disappears next to declared initializers); an internal struct without initializers keeps the implicit one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An enum is cloned as a whole and listed without properties. It is serialized only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" itself, and it gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"DefaultInitializable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The macro stores "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let componentIndex = registeredComponentIndex"},{"type":"text","text":". The index still comes from the registry at first access, so it cannot collide with a lazily assigned one. Declare your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"componentIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" to opt out."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Value types and diagnostics","anchor":"Value-types-and-diagnostics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports an error when it is applied to a class: components are value types, so use a struct or enum. The nexus also asserts once per component type, in debug builds, that a hand-written conformance is not a class."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stored property spelled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Entity"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Entity?"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Entity]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Set<Entity>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"[Key: Entity]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an error with a fix-it that replaces ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityIdentifier"},{"text":". An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity"},{"text":" keeps its nexus alive and is not valid after a copy, a clone or a snapshot, while an identifier is a plain value that the clone context remaps. The macro sees syntax only: an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behind a typealias or in a nested type is not diagnosed and stays a convention.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Registering-cloning-and-snapshots","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Registering, cloning and snapshots"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()","try nexus.register([Transform.self, RenderHandle.self])","","\/\/ Clone a whole world; entity references (`parent`) are remapped to the clones.","let playMode = Nexus()","try nexus.clone(into: playMode)","","\/\/ Export and import all serializable components, keyed by their stable type names.","var encoder = JSONEncoder()","let data = try nexus.encodeSnapshot(using: &encoder, handling: .skip)","var decoder = JSONDecoder()","try playMode.decodeSnapshot(from: data, using: &decoder)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component types are registered automatically the first time an instance is assigned."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Register them explicitly before decoding snapshots that reference them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" starts with a "},{"code":"formatVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and keeps the original entity identifiers.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Decoding creates new entities, remaps entity references to them through an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityReferenceResolver"},{"text":", and rejects snapshots written in a newer format version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Fi